        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Orders Allocated By Wave"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764709899292"
          },
          "code": "ORDERS_ALLOCATED_BY_WAVE",
          "id": "1764113420010",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764113420012_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role: Your role is to act as a wave researcher. You will be provided an  \nOrder Number : {{$context.$nodes.SET_INITIAL_VARIABLES.$input.OrderNumber}} \n WaveNumber: {{$context.$nodes.SET_INITIAL_VARIABLES.$input.WaveNumber}} \n\n\n**Order Status interpretation\n\nstatus_id - Description\n0-Created\n10-Partly Allocated\n20-Allocated\n25-In Picking\n27-Picked\n30-In Packing\n40-Packed\n50-Loaded\n90-Shipped\n99-Cancelled\n\n**Allocation Status Interpretation \nstatus_id - Description\n0-Allocated\n30-Processing started\n90-Completed\n99-Cancelled\n\nStep 1: Retrieve Order Information {{$context.$nodes.GETORDERHEADER.$output}}\n\nStep 2: Retrieve Order detail information , allocated by wave number\n {{$context.$nodes.GETORDERDTLALLOCATEDBYWAVE.$output}}\nThis retrieves the order details allocate by  {{$context.$nodes.SET_INITIAL_VARIABLES.$input.WaveNumber}} \n\nStep 3: Retrieve the allocation of order\n {{$context.$nodes.GETALLOCATIONSBYORDER.$output}} \nThis retrieves the allocations created by the order {{$context.$nodes.SET_INITIAL_VARIABLES.$input.OrderNumber}} \n\n\nStep 4: Exclude cancelled allocations\nidentify the status of the allocations from step 3. If the status_id is 99. Do not include those allocations when calculating the Order Allocated quantity\n\nStep 5: Order status interpretations and allocation:\nif order status  is created status_id=0 :\nIf allocated quantity is 0, but a wave selected the order, inform the user that the wave selected the order, but it was not allocated.\nIf there is no record, inform the user the order has not been picked up by any wave.\nIf order status is above Created:\nThe order was selected/allocated by a wave.\nTo verify which wave, compare the wave number in the allocations with the wave entered by the user.\n\nif the allocated quantity is zero this means the order has selected by the wave, but it could not be allocated.\nIf there is not a record, the order has not been picked up by a wave.\n\nif the order has a status_id >0\nThe order has been selected and allocated by a wave.\nTo verify which wave allocated the order.\n  \nlook at the output from {{$context.$nodes.GETALLOCATIONSBYORDER.$output}} \ncompare the Wave Number in the allocation vs the WaveNumber the user entered.  \n\n\n\n** calculate the following\nOrder Original quantity: {{$context.$nodes.GETALLOCATIONSBYORDER.$output}}  group all the order details  of an ordered and sum the order_dtl_id__orig_ord_qty. Only sum order_dtl_id__orig_ord_qty for unique order_dtl_id within each order.\nOrder Allocated quantity:  {{$context.$nodes.GETALLOCATIONSBYORDER.$output}}  group all the order details  of an ordered and sum the order_dtl_id__alloc_qty  only group allocations with status_id<99\ncompare the two result and create a 1 sentence summary - called it {ord_vs_alloc}\n\n\n<strong>Order Number <strong> : order_number  \nAllocated by Wave provided : allocated_by_wave_provided\nAllocated Wave: allocated_by_wave\nOrder Status: order_status\nTotal Quantity allocated: sum order_dtl_id__alloc_qty and  ordered_uom \nTotal Order quantity : sum of order_dtl_id__orig_ord_qty  and ordered_uom \nTotal Task Created : total_tasks_created\nOther:[If the  status_id=0 and the order was selected by a wave but not allocated. inform user the wave that selected but not allocated wave ]\n\n\n**Notes\nDo not add status_id just the description\nuse ordered_uom key when refering to uom\n\n\"Filter your allocations to exclude those where status_id is 99 before performing any aggregation/count logic.\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"order_number\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Unique identifier for the order.\"\n    },\n    \"allocated_by_wave_provided\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Are wave provided and allocated wave the same\"\n    },\n    \"wave_provided\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Wave Number provided by user.\"\n    },\n    \"allocated_by_wave\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Actual wave allocated. It could be multiple.\"\n    },\n    \"order_status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Current status of the order.\"\n    },\n    \"Order Ship Date\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Current status of the order.\"\n    },\n    \"Total Quantity allocated\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"description\": \"Order Total quantity allocated.\"\n    },\n \"UOM\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"description\": \"quantity uom.\"\n    },\n   \"Total Order quantity\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"description\": \"Order quantity.\"\n    },\n \"UOM\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"description\": \"quantity uom.\"\n    },\n    \"total_tasks_created\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"description\": \"Total number of tasks created for the order.\"\n    },\n   \"other\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"information if order was selected by a wave but not allocated.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"order_number\",\n    \"allocated_by_wave_provided\",\n    \"wave_provided\",\n    \"allocated_by_wave\",\n    \"order_status\",\n    \"total_tasks_created\",\n    \"Total Quantity allocated\",\n   \"Total Order quantity\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
